[38;2;124;124;124mLet me also verify the claim that $\mathbb{F}_{q^m} \subseteq F'$ iff $m$ is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpower of 2. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$F' = \bigcup_k \mathbb{F}_{q^{2^k}}$. The field $\mathbb{F}_{q^m}$ is contained[0m[38;2;124;124;124min $\mathbb{F}_{q^{2^k}}$ iff $m | 2^k$. So $\mathbb{F}_{q^m} \subseteq F'$ iff [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthere exists $k$ with $m | 2^k$, iff $m$ is a power of 2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $3$ is not a power of $2$, $\mathbb{F}_{q^3} \not\subseteq F'$, but $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{F}_{q^3} \subseteq \overline{F}$. So $F' \subsetneq \overline{F}$. ✓[0m

